          },
          "id": "4189392774"
        },
        "body": "An unquoted value with `(`, `[`, `{`, `<` or `>` in the middle is rejected whole, so the secret is sent unredacted. For example, `DB_PASSWORD=aB3xY9kLm2(z!` stops at `(`, which is not in the end set. Generated passwords often contain these characters. A `,`, `;` or `&` in the middle redacts the prefix, so the two cases behave differently. The \"Known limits\" in the MR description do not mention this case, and no test covers it. Is rejecting the whole value intended? If so, please list it as a known limit and add a test. Otherwise redact up to the stop character, as `,` is handled."
      },
      "summary": "GitLabDuo commented",
      "threadSnapshot": {
        "title": "feat(govern): redact values assigned to credential-like names in text"
      },
      "occurredAt": "<now>",
